// src/v4/workflow/ci.dag
//
// Scope: CI pipeline AS DATA. .github/workflows/ci.yml becomes a DERIVED artifact emitted from this file. Adding a CI gate = editing this one .dag file (THESIS:226). v3's gate #98 ci_yml_hand_authority_dissolved was an open R3 gap precisely because CI YAML was hand-authored — v4 must NOT reproduce it.
// Anchor: THESIS:223-226 (meta-process modeling: "Bootstrap, CI ... modeled as .dag workflows") + v4-close-interrogation.md §3.2 (ci_workflow_modeled_as_dag) + v3 gate #98 (the gap v4 must not reproduce)
//
// Owns:
//   - CiPipeline { jobs: List<CiJob>, gates: List<CiGate> }
//   - affected-set-driven job selection: consumes lens/affected_set.dag
//     (this is what replaces scripts/detect-affected-components.sh — the
//     shell bridge dissolves once this + affected_set land)
//   - emission target: .github/workflows/ci.yml as DERIVED artifact (Shape B
//     user-program emission — .dag walks CiPipeline, emits YAML)
//   - C4 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15): the committed `ci.yml` MUST exist
//     on disk (GitHub reads it from the repo) yet is NOT editable
//     authority. It is a committed == emit(CiPipeline) CHECKED PROJECTION,
//     guarded by the SAME machine as A3: if committed ci.yml ≠
//     emit(CiPipeline), CI is red and the divergence is conspicuous +
//     STOP-routed. This is how feedback_no_generated_code_on_disk is
//     honored honestly — "no editable generated AUTHORITY", not "no
//     generated bytes on disk". The `.dag` is authority; the file is a
//     checked projection.
//   - cache keys in the emitted `ci.yml` are STRUCTURAL: each cacheable
//     job's `actions/cache` key is `content_hash` (B1) of that job's
//     input subgraph, derived from the dependency graph via
//     lens/affected_set.dag — not a hand-authored `hashFiles(...)` glob.
//     GHA `actions/cache` is one emission target of that hash; a remote
//     build cache is another. The interim hand-written `hashFiles(...)`
//     keys in the committed `ci.yml` (e.g. the v2-compiler-binary cache)
//     are manual approximations of those content-hashes; emitting
//     `ci.yml` from this file replaces them with the real structural keys.
//
// Consumes:
//   - lens/affected_set.dag: job selection
//   - extdeps/process.dag: CI steps spawn subprocesses
//   - workflow/bootstrap.dag: CI runs the bootstrap chain
//
// Status: filled (declarative core — T-24 structural-gate slice). The
// CiPipeline job/gate-DAG shape + the affected-set-selection seam are
// present and v2-compile-clean. The C4 ci.yml projection is NOT a
// present property of this data — it is BLOCKED on missing GHA
// workflow-schema substrate and surfaced for operator confirmation
// (see HONEST SCOPE OF THE C4 CLAIM + TRACKED SCAFFOLD (1)); the
// committed ci.yml stays the explicit interim hand-authored bridge
// meanwhile. The canonical `ci_pipeline` instance models the
// structural v2-compile gate (the existing day-1 CI gate: v2 indexes
// src/v4). The ci.yml PROJECTION body, affected-set SELECTION body, and
// the executable test/eval jobs are DEFERRED — see TRACKED SCAFFOLD.
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// DATA, not a runner. `CiPipeline` is the gunbc CI pipeline AS DATA:
// the job/gate dependency DAG (the affected-set-selection surface —
// the load-bearing T-24 concern) as inert structure. The
// `.github/workflows/ci.yml` C4 projection is the eventual goal; v3's
// gate #98 `ci_yml_hand_authority_dissolved` was an open R3 gap and v4
// must not reproduce it.
//
// HONEST SCOPE OF THE C4 CLAIM (INVARIANTS P1 — no fabrication; the
// affected_set.dag `detect-affected-components.sh` interim-bridge
// precedent). A FAITHFUL `.github/workflows/ci.yml` requires GitHub
// Actions WORKFLOW-SCHEMA facts — `on:` triggers, per-job `runs-on:`
// runners, the `steps:` list (checkout/setup/run), concurrency,
// permissions (workflow-syntax spec) — that `CiPipeline { jobs,
// gates }` deliberately does NOT carry: those are the GHA TRANSPORT,
// not the gunbc job/gate DAG. A `CiPipeline -> ci.yml` projection over
// only jobs/gates would therefore have to FABRICATE every trigger,
// runner, and step (an INVARIANTS P1/P2 violation — the exact review
// finding). It is NOT fabricated here because no projection is
// authored: the GHA workflow schema is MISSING SUBSTRATE in v4 (v3's
// `extdeps/github/actions.dag` `Workflow/Job/Step/Trigger/...` model
// has NO v4 counterpart; minting one is a NEW extdeps file =
// substrate extension = operator-tier, NOT a worker add — STOP, not
// improvise). UNTIL that substrate exists, the committed
// `.github/workflows/ci.yml` REMAINS the explicit INTERIM HAND-AUTHORED
// BRIDGE — exactly as `scripts/detect-affected-components.sh` is the
// declared interim bridge for affected_set (lens/affected_set.dag
// header) — and the `committed == emit(...)` CHECKED-PROJECTION C4
// state is explicitly a FUTURE state gated on the named missing
// substrate, with an owner (TRACKED SCAFFOLD (1)), not a property
// claimed of the present `{ jobs, gates }` data.
//
// HEADER TENSION — SURFACED, not silently reinterpreted. The immutable
// scaffold header (Owns / C4) binds BOTH the `CiPipeline { jobs,
// gates }` shape AND "committed == emit(CiPipeline) CHECKED
// PROJECTION" of `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Those two are in tension:
// the projection cannot be faithful over jobs/gates alone (above).
// Resolving it needs either a GHA-workflow-schema extdeps model (new
// file, operator-tier) feeding the projection, or an operator decision
// to narrow the C4-over-CiPipeline header claim. Per the
// frozen-scaffold-header ratification discipline this worker does NOT
// edit the immutable Owns/C4 lines; the tension is flagged on the PR
// for conscious operator confirmation. This note is the honest
// tracked statement of the gap, not a convention papering it.
//
// WHY job/gate edges are `Symbol`, not inlined sub-nodes. `CiJob.needs`
// and `CiGate.job` are post-resolution opaque `Symbol` references
// (std/node.dag, K-1) to job ids — a job-dependency DAG by NAME, never
// producer-inlining (project_v4_ssa_name_reference_not_inlining: a cyclic
// or shared dependency graph cannot be finitely represented by
// inlining). Affected-set selection (TRACKED SCAFFOLD (2)) traverses
// these `Symbol` edges exactly as lens/affected_set.dag derives its
// graph by `Symbol`-equality traversal.
//
// WHY `command` is an opaque `String`. A job's command line is a leaf
// lexeme the deferred CI interpreter (extdeps/process.dag) executes —
// modeled like yaml.dag's scalar `lexeme: String` (the structural cache
// key + process spawn are the deferred operation, not a stored field).
// It is job DATA, not a string sentinel: nothing branches on its
// contents within this substrate.
//
// TRACKED SCAFFOLD (🟡) — operations deferred with owner + trigger, per
// the operator-ratified declarative-now / operations-deferred discipline
// (std/collection.dag #3169, canonical json.dag #3184). NOT improvised
// bodies, NOT bodiless `fn` (frozen v2 rejects bodiless `fn`, DECISIONS
// PARSE-1):
//   (1) `project_ci_yml : (CiPipeline, GhaWorkflowSchema) ->
//       Outcome<YamlValue>` — the C4 projection. It CANNOT be a
//       `CiPipeline -> ci.yml` function: the gunbc job/gate DAG alone
//       lacks the GHA workflow-schema transport (`on`/`runs-on`/
//       `steps`/concurrency/permissions), so a faithful projection
//       MUST also consume a GitHub Actions workflow-schema model that
//       supplies those transport facts (the gunbc data fills the
//       schema; it never invents it — no fabrication, INVARIANTS P1).
//       FAIL-CLOSED (`Outcome<T>`, std/diagnostic.dag, DECISIONS item
//       I), mirroring the ratified `yaml_emit : YamlValue ->
//       Outcome<String>` seam #3. Then committed
//       `.github/workflows/ci.yml` becomes a `committed == emit(...)`
//       CHECKED PROJECTION (C4 / STRUCTURE.md invariant 7); UNTIL THEN
//       the committed file is the explicit interim hand-authored bridge
//       (see HONEST SCOPE OF THE C4 CLAIM above).
//       OWNER/TRIGGER: BLOCKED on MISSING SUBSTRATE — a GitHub Actions
//       workflow-schema extdeps model (no v4 counterpart to v3's
//       `extdeps/github/actions.dag`; a NEW file = operator-tier
//       substrate extension, surfaced on the PR, NOT added here). Then
//       additionally needs extdeps/formats/yaml.dag `yaml_emit`
//       (T-4.6) + compiler/05_emit.dag (T-10) Shape-B emission.
//   (2) `select_jobs : (CiPipeline, Diff) -> List<CiJob>` — affected-set
//       job selection, consuming lens/affected_set.dag's `affected_set :
//       (Dag, Diff) -> Witness<ReExecFrontier>` (this is IB-2 / what
//       dissolves scripts/detect-affected-components.sh). lens/
//       affected_set.dag is T-21 SCAFFOLD (zero declarations today) — no
//       `affected_set` / `ReExecFrontier` symbol exists to consume yet,
//       so the selection body is not authored (scaffold-header drift
//       discipline: reference the seam, defer the body).
//       OWNER/TRIGGER: dissolves when lens/affected_set.dag (T-21) lands.
//   (3) The executable per-job evaluation (running fmt/clippy/test jobs,
//       structural cache restore/store keyed by `content_hash` B1) rides
//       compiler/05_eval.dag + extdeps/process.dag.
//       OWNER/TRIGGER: T-22 (eval) + T-4.5 (process). Until then the
//       ONLY exercised gate is structural: this file v2-compiles as
//       well-formed data, and `v2_compile_gate_job` models that existing
//       day-1 CI gate concretely (not theater — it is the real gate).
//
// `CiPipeline` is a Conj record over closed Disj-free records; no
// Practice-4 ledger applies (records do not dissolve to a richer
// source — the diagnostic.dag `Diagnostic` / verification.dag
// `TestClaim` precedent).

module v4.workflow.ci


import v4.std.node { Symbol }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CiJob — one CI job. `id` is its opaque identity; `needs` are the job
// ids it depends on (the job DAG, traversed by `Symbol` equality);
// `command` is the leaf command line the deferred interpreter runs.
type CiJob {
  id: Symbol
  command: String
  needs: List<Symbol>
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CiGate — a required check: the pipeline is GREEN only if the job
// named `job` succeeds. Gates are the affected-set/STOP surface (a
// failing gate is conspicuous and STOP-routed, A3 machine).
type CiGate {
  id: Symbol
  job: Symbol
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CiPipeline — the gunbc job/gate dependency DAG AS DATA (the
// affected-set-selection surface). It is NOT, by itself, a present C4
// authority for `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: the faithful projection
// also needs a GHA workflow-schema model for the transport facts
// jobs/gates deliberately omit (TRACKED SCAFFOLD (1) + HONEST SCOPE OF
// THE C4 CLAIM above). Affected-set selection over `jobs` is TRACKED
// SCAFFOLD (2).
type CiPipeline {
  jobs: List<CiJob>
  gates: List<CiGate>
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Job/gate identities. `Symbol` is opaque (K-1, no spelling accessor);
// a Symbol value is a declared name (std/integer.dag reason-symbol
// precedent: `data x: Symbol = x`).
data v2_compile_src_v4: Symbol = v2_compile_src_v4
data structural_v2_compile: Symbol = structural_v2_compile


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The structural v2-compile gate — the existing day-1 CI gate modeled
// concretely: v2 indexes/compiles src/v4 (the parse-viability step that
// keeps the .dag corpus v2-bridge-clean). This is the ONLY job
// exercised today; the executable test/eval lane is TRACKED SCAFFOLD
// (3), deferred to T-22.
data v2_compile_gate_job: CiJob = CiJob {
  id: v2_compile_src_v4,
  command: "v2-compiler compile --source-root src/v4",
  needs: []
}

data ci_pipeline: CiPipeline = CiPipeline {
  jobs: [v2_compile_gate_job],
  gates: [
    CiGate { id: structural_v2_compile, job: v2_compile_src_v4 }
  ]
}

